        "original_id": "78bfd069-a370-5039-af75-00616c9f8587",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 59th Primetime Emmy Awards\n- Companies: Fox Broadcasting Company, Fox Entertainment Group, 21st Century Fox\n- Places: Shrine Auditorium, Los Angeles, California, Century City, West Los Angeles, Manhattan, New York City\n\nFacts:\n- The 59th Primetime Emmy Awards were held on Sunday, September 16, 2007, at the Shrine Auditorium in Los Angeles, California.\n- The 59th Primetime Emmy Awards honored the best in U.S. prime time television programming.\n- The 59th Primetime Emmy Awards were televised live on Fox at 8:00 p.m. EDT and aired on a three-hour tape delay on the U.S. West Coast at 8:00 p.m.\n- The 59th Primetime Emmy Awards were televised for the first time in high definition.\n- Fox Broadcasting Company is an American commercial broadcast television network often shortened to Fox and stylized as FOX.\n- Fox Broadcasting Company is owned by Fox Entertainment Group, which is a subsidiary of 21st Century Fox.\n- Fox Broadcasting Company is headquartered at the 20th Century Fox studio on Pico Boulevard in Century City, Los Angeles.\n- Fox Broadcasting Company has additional major offices and production facilities at the Fox Television Center in West Los Angeles and the Fox Broadcasting Center in Yorkville, Manhattan, New York City.",
